{"name":"Steampunk Leather","hex":"#6f3b34","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"steampunk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A subgenre of science fiction that depicts advanced technology combined with Victorian style and aesthetics, such as steam-powered machines and vehicles, visible gears and screws and people dressed in 19th-century attires.","A writer of steampunk fiction."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To depict in a steampunk manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steampunk"},{"term":"leather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tough material produced from the skin of animals, by tanning or similar process, used e.g. for clothing; often denotes leather from cattle when no qualifier specifies otherwise.","A piece of the above used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of leather.","Referring to one who wears leather clothing (motorcycle jacket, chaps over 501 jeans, boots), especially as a sign of sadomasochistic homosexuality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Steampunk","blocks":[{"text":"Steampunk is a subgenre of science fiction that incorporates retro-futuristic technology and aesthetics prominently inspired by 19th-century industrial steam-powered machinery and design. Steampunk works are often set in an alternative history of the Victorian era and the Belle Époque, or the American frontier where steam power remains in mainstream use, or in a fantasy world that similarly employs steam power."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/20000_Nautilus_engines.jpg/330px-20000_Nautilus_engines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steampunk"},{"title":"Leather","blocks":[{"text":"Leather is a strong, flexible and durable material obtained from the tanning, or chemical treatment, of animal skins and hides to prevent decay. The 